  "limitations": [
    "The cache stores only T=1 and T=4 readouts; depths T=2,3 were never measured, so G uses the two endpoints only.",
    "Document identity is exact doc_id only: no near-duplicate / group-level near hash (e.g. MinHash) exists in this cache, so near-duplicate leakage between controller_train and newtest cannot be excluded beyond the verified empty exact doc_id intersection; this analysis does not fabricate such a hash.",
    "All metrics are on previously viewed newtest states (diagnostic, not a confirmation split).",
    "A large interaction I or depth gain G does not imply a deploy benefit; only D at the final depth is deploy-relevant, and every D here is orders of magnitude below the oracle gap."
  ],
  "conclusion": {
    "stable": true,
    "interpretation": "candidate_rank has a large interaction (I=0.1464) but a final-depth deploy difference D=-0.000512 whose doc-level 95% CI crosses zero; constant_global has a statistically positive but tiny improvement (-D=0.000464, 95% CI excludes zero); uniform expectation is worse than baseline. Large G/I is a mechanism statement, not deploy value.",
    "t2_t3_recommendation": "Not warranted for a deployment claim: the largest deploy-relevant effect (constant_global, ~4.6e-4 nats, ~0.009% of baseline cost) is far below practical relevance and 1.3% of the label-informed oracle gap; a <=1024-state T2/T3 confirmation would at most re-verify a negligible D. If run anyway for sign stability, cap it at <=1024 states on a fresh split and pre-register D, not G/I, as the endpoint."
  }
